    result: "An agent that converts by being trustworthy, handing off before it guesses and recovering cleanly when it cannot help.",
    storyThroughLine: "The easy version of this agent answers questions. The hard version knows what it is not allowed to say and refuses gracefully instead of guessing or leaking something confidential. I expected the guardrails to be the part I would hide, a necessary constraint bolted onto the product. Instead I published them, and it turned out that watching the agent decline something teaches a visitor more about how the practice thinks than a good answer would. Before it shipped, I ran it against twenty adversarial and functional tests, jailbreak attempts included, and held the bar at a full pass rather than a good-enough one.",
